# What a local `docker build` leaves out of its context.
#
# The add-on image copies `configs/` whole. A working checkout also holds the `ref_`
# templates generated at every start, user clones and their history databases, and
# `configs/.secrets/` and `configs/rates/`, which hold credentials and API keys. Git
# tracks none of them, so a build from git never sees them; this keeps a local build
# the same. Only the tracked templates and presets go in. tests/test_dockerignore.py
# reads these rules as Docker does.
configs/*
!configs/presets
!configs/ref_MAIN_32_TANDEMS.yaml
!configs/ref_MLO_48_TANDEMS.yaml

# Local state and caches, none of which the image uses.
.env
.git
.local
.venv
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.superpowers
**/__pycache__
